          <attvalue for="35" value="A fall in US–Canada bilateral trade volumes disrupts cross‑border movement of defense components and munitions (including North American production runs and transit routes), directly reducing the throughput of deliveries destined for Ukraine and thus lowering the defensive asset resupply rate." />
